# App router (`apps/web/src/app`)

Only Next.js route files live here: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, `template.tsx`, `route.ts`, and other [supported route files](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/file-conventions).

No module components, hooks, utils, or thin client wrappers under `app/`. UI lives in `client/modules/`; `page.tsx` and `layout.tsx` import it.

```tsx
// layout.tsx — server layout composes a module client component
import { AppSidebar } from "@/client/modules/shared/ui/app-sidebar/components/app-sidebar";

export default async function Layout({ children }: PropsWithChildren) {
  const session = await auth();
  return <AppSidebar user={session?.user}>{children}</AppSidebar>;
}
```

# Page

Default export is `Page`. Put `"use client"` on the page when the route is client-only; module children under it don't repeat it.

```tsx
"use client";

import { Skeleton } from "@workspace/design-system/components/ui/skeleton";
import { Suspense } from "react";

import { OnboardingSteps } from "@/client/modules/onboarding/components/onboarding-steps";

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<Skeleton className="h-100" />}>
      <OnboardingSteps />
    </Suspense>
  );
}
```

## Data

Wrap the part of the tree that suspends. Fallback: a design-system `Skeleton`, or omit it and let `app/loading.tsx` (global spinner) cover the route.

## Composing modules

Modules meet on the page. The page composes them; never re-export a component from another module (no `export { InviteBanner } from "..."` inside `auth`).

```tsx
export default function Page() {
  return (
    <>
      <SignInForm />
      <InviteBanner token={token} />
    </>
  );
}
```
